irst deposited model) is used uniformly. Ensemble-wide agreement is a separate question this stratum does not test."}},"official_metric_import":{"by_stratum":{"alphafold":{"evidence_source":"alphafold_db_confidence","note":"No wwPDB validation report exists for a predicted model. The official confidence evidence is pLDDT in the B-factor column plus the PAE matrix, so the gate checks those instead of geometry-validation metrics.","required_confidence":["state","mean_angstrom","max_angstrom","size"],"required_metrics":[]},"cryo_em":{"evidence_source":"wwpdb_validation_report","note":"A cryo-EM validation report carries the same geometry metrics as an x-ray one plus a reported resolution, but no crystallographic R-factors. Resolution is required here because the report supplies it; requiring r_free would fail every case in the stratum.","required_metrics":["clashscore","ramachandran_outliers_percent","rotamer_outliers_percent","resolution_angstrom"]},"nmr":{"evidence_source":"wwpdb_validation_report","note":"A solution-NMR validation report carries geometry metrics but neither resolution nor R-factors, because neither exists for the method. The metric set is the geometry core alone.","required_metrics":["clashscore","ramachandran_outliers_percent","rotamer_outliers_percent"]},"x_ray":{"evidence_source":"wwpdb_validation_report","required_metrics":["clashscore","ramachandran_outliers_percent","rotamer_outliers_percent"]}},"mode":"exact"},"residue_identity":{"alternatives":{"equals_one":"Identity must be 1.0 for every case. Disqualifies every structure carrying an engineered mutation, including 2V7A, and with it the panel's only nonstandard-residue coverage.","matches_declared_expectation":"The computed identity must equal the value declared for the case. A declared engineered mutation is expected to lower identity, and failing to lower it is the defect."},"chosen_because":"2V7A measures 0.996296, which is exactly 1 - 1/270: the single declared T315I difference and nothi